[12/13/14/15 Regression] Path splitting causes if-conversion miss
Similar toPR 68541except instead of having a diamond, we just have a triangle.

Testcase:
```
int
foo(signed char *p, int n)
{
  int s = 0;
  int i;

  for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    int t;
    if (p[i] >= 0)
      t=1;
    else
      t=-1;
    s+=t;
  }

  return s;
}
```

I noticed this while working on fixingPR 94274.
